'''Arrabád''' (from [[W:Arabic|Arabic]] الرَّبَض; ''rabád''; {{Literally|suburb|slum}}) is a [[Communes of Balisca|barrio]] of the [[Llanito]] borough, within the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. It contains the largest and most well known [[W:Red-light district|red-light district]] in the Metropolis. It is considered to be an area historically infamous for its permissive underground/counterculture (including [[W:Cabarets|cabarets]], [[W:Neo burlesque|neo-burlesque]], [[W:Drag shows|drag shows]]) as well as [[W:Brothel|brothels]], [[W:Hammam|hammams]]/bathhouses and petty crime (typically [[W:Pickpocketing|pickpocketing]]), earning Arrabád the moniker "[[W:Barbary Coast, San Francisco|Barbary Coast]]".  

It currently has a very diverse immigrant community (52.3% of its population was born abroad, ranging from Indians, South Americans, and Sugihans, to a more recent [[W:Afghan diaspora|Afghan community]]). Arrabád has been undergoing significant population growth in recent years, and there has been discontent with attempts to give the barrio a more "[[W:Family friendly|family friendly]]" image, leading to some to call for the area to be declared a [[W:No kid zone|no kid zone]]. 

